{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774708,"nonce":"MHWcQbF4KM1lLsJibj50VT5/StE=","title":"invoke + named results + egress sidecar (ADR-0038, 0041, 0042)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #4 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0038-invoke` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-14T14:42:04Z · Merged: 2026-07-14T14:48:48Z\n\nThree stacked, dependency-ordered ADRs that together add local composition and make step outputs flow.\n\n`invoke: .scarab/lib/x.yaml` is resolved by **compile-time inlining**, not a runtime object: the referenced pipeline's steps are flattened into the caller's DAG, id-namespaced by the invoke-step id (`deploy/build`), with `needs` rewritten across the seam. Purity holds (ADR-0031) — the server pre-fetches lib sources and hands a `{path→source}` map to a pure `compile_yaml_with_libs`.\n- **Slice 1** — step kind + single-level inlining + path safety (no absolute / `..` / cross-repo).\n- **Slice 2** — recursive nesting (`deploy/db/migrate`), cycle detection (offending path in the diagnostic), depth cap; transitive lib fetch.\n- **Slice 3** — explicit `interface: { inputs, outputs }`; caller `with:` → `SCARAB_PARAM_*`; compile-validated.\n- **Slice 4** — `matrix` × `invoke` fan-out (one subgraph copy per coordinate; `exclude` honored).\n\nAll four git-bug issues closed.\n\nMakes 0038's `outputs` **live**. Results are a typed per-step `name → JSON value` map (`step_runs.results`, migration 0018); a downstream `${{ outputs.\u003cstep\u003e.\u003cname\u003e }}` is resolved **at launch** from upstream results (the first `${{ }}` interpolation pass). Compile rewrites invoke-output refs to the concrete inlined step so the runtime context stays generic. **Fail-fast/fail-closed**: undeclared/no-`needs`/matrixed-invoke references are compile errors; a missing result or a type-mismatched guard fails the step — never an empty render. Local backend captures end-to-end.\n\nResults are *data* (must not be lost), so they ride an **acknowledged** channel, not the best-effort k8s log stream. A trusted per-Pod **sidecar** (native sidecar: initContainer, `restartPolicy: Always`) shares a `/scarab/results` emptyDir with the untrusted step and does a confirmed write to a **fence-scoped results API → Postgres**. The sidecar holds the `HMAC(secret, run:step:attempt)` token; the untrusted step holds none (preserves ADR-0038 isolation). Rationale (in \"Alternatives considered\"): k8s logs are lossy, stdout markers are an injection surface (GHA CVE-2020-15228 → files), Events/termination-message/etcd are lossy or split the source of truth off Postgres, and a node-driver / full runner-agent reintroduce an agent without a delivery guarantee.\n\n`cargo test --workspace` → **226 passed, 4 ignored** (cluster live-runs), `cargo clippy` clean. Includes an in-memory end-to-end value chain (producer result → consumer interpolation) and fail-fast, the server ingest endpoint (token/paths), and the k8s pod-shape wiring.\n\nThe **k8s egress sidecar image** (the `scarab` CLI that drains `/scarab/results` and POSTs on shutdown) and a **real-cluster lifecycle test** — this environment can't build an image or run a cluster. The receiving half (ingest API + token) and the Pod-spec wiring are implemented and unit-tested; the local backend captures results end-to-end today. Also deferred per ADR-0041: matrix/event interpolation (same rail) and matrixed-invoke output references.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}